WEBVTT

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.160
A chance to drive in a run and it's Komori, huh?

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:08.910
This is pretty bad from the get-go.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:12.050
<i>The balls are faster and sharper than in the first game,</i>

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.840
<i>but the variety and patterns are according to the data.</i>

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:16.960
<i>It hasn't changed so much that it's troublesome.</i>

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.050
<i>Sorry, but...</i>

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.510
<i>I'll be taking this one!</i>

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:26.750
Foul!

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.440
<i>He's small, but he's got power.</i>

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.330
<i>Fastballs are too dangerous.</i>

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.860
<i>Let's go with an outside curve that'll look like a ball.</i>

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:39.600
<i>It's fine if we give them one base.</i>

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.030
<i>What?</i>

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.660
<i>If that's the case, a fastball's fine. Just make sure that it misses!</i>

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:52.150
<i>The next one will probably be a breaking ball outside or a ball.</i>

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.120
<i>If it enters the strike zone, I'll get it this time!</i>

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:03.330
Out!

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:04.760
Three outs! Change!

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:08.470
<i>A fastball... inside?</i>

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:10.760
<i>That guy...</i>

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:12.470
<i>He's pretty good!</i>

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:16.430
<i>He was strong-willed and knew what Komori was thinking!</i>

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:18.600
Bottom of the fourth inning: leading off for Mifune High School...

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:22.810
Batting second: second baseman, Ihara-kun.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.610
Let's go and get some runs this inning.

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:26.520
Yes sir!

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:28.360
Play!

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:34.670
<i>Second time around, huh?</i>

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:37.790
<i>It's about time they started doing something.</i>

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:46.210
Third!

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:48.130
Damn!

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:50.420
Safe! Safe!

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:51.970
Safe! Safe!

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:55.720
All right! Good going, Ihara!

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:01.370
<i>Right from the start, they didn't target Taiga, who's good at fielding,</i>

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:03.520
<i>but aimed a bunt at Uchiyama?</i>

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.730
<i>On top of the fact that they've researched us,</i>

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:10.610
<i>they're seriously coming to score some runs this inning.</i>

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:15.070
Batting third: first baseman, Oobayashi-kun.

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:20.580
<i>This guy... The last time he batted, he almost got a hit off the curve, right?</i>

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:32.050
<i>What?</i>

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:33.260
It's a hit and run!

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:44.610
All right! No outs and runners on first and third!

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:50.560
<i>That Oobayashi...</i>

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:53.630
<i>Since when has he been able to bat so skillfully?</i>

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:57.990
Batting fourth: catcher, Komori-kun.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:01.210
<i>I'm not letting them have one run.</i>

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:04.000
<i>If we allow this opponent to score a single run, we'll...</i>

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:05.790
<i>be finished!</i>

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:14.460
Stop!

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:15.540
Safe!

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.900
All right! We've got the first run!

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:33.110
The first run...

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:35.150
Got taken from us...

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:43.200
Batting fifth: pitcher, Yamane-kun.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:48.670
Damn!

00:05:58.350 --> 00:05:59.050
Two runs!

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:01.320
A three run lead in one breath!

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.640
Nice job, Yamane!

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:12.940
Oh no...

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:16.640
<i>T-This is Mifune's ability, huh?</i>

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:20.960
Ball! Four balls!

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:26.560
All right! Go!

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:28.660
We can still get more runs this inning!

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:33.130
Batting seventh: right fielder, Hamaoka-kun.

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.490
Get a hold of yourself, Taiga!

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.300
It's only a three-run difference halfway through the game!

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:38.840
Don't give up!

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:44.290
All right!

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:44.290
All right!

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:45.940
One down, runners on first and second!

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:49.950
<i>This is bad!</i>

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:53.270
<i>He's completely losing his concentration.</i>

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:56.550
A first-year pitcher with little experience, huh?

00:06:57.880 --> 00:06:59.490
It's the same as the first game.

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:03.860
He's the type that can't stay motivated once he gets shaken up.

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:13.070
<i>I'm telling you that if you're mortified about it,
start producing some results.</i>

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:16.630
<i>It's because you're all talk that no one trusts you.</i>

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:19.100
<i>You got it, right, Taiga?</i>

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:23.640
<i>Without your cooperation, it's impossible for Seishuu to win and keep going!</i>

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:28.640
<i>How pathetic.</i>

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:32.280
<i>In the end, this is the limit of my skills.</i>

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:36.110
<i>I actually got motivated by the fact that senpai was using freezing and became serious.</i>

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:38.190
<i>How uncool...</i>

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:42.030
<i>I just want to hurry home and continue playing some games...</i>

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:49.870
Out!

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:52.330
Three outs! Change!

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:55.590
They did it! A double play!

00:07:56.260 --> 00:07:59.980
Wait a second. How am I supposed to score that last play?

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:02.790
Sorry, Taiga.

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:07.560
Thanks to my clumsiness and my inability to field the bunt, I broke your rhythm.

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:09.260
That was...

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:13.660
With that last play we can't recover the three runs we've lost, but it's still the fifth inning.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:16.080
Let's not give up, and do our best!

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:19.870
Nice, third, Uchiyama!

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:21.680
You did well!

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:25.610
It was luck, luck!

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.370
You...

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:32.830
Top of the fifth inning: leading off for Seishuu High School...

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:36.630
Batting sixth: first baseman, Miyazaki-kun.

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:41.010
Strike!

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:43.250
You can hit it, you can hit it!

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:45.050
Choose the good pitches and swing!

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:48.660
<i>Not give up?</i>

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:52.020
<i>But the opponent's different from our first game.</i>

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:55.350
Foul!

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:56.800
<i>I-I hit it...</i>

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:57.940
<i>I-I hit it...</i>

00:08:57.940 --> 00:08:58.980
Keep trying!

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:01.480
Good job, Miyazaki! Don't give up!

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:04.900
Ball!

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:08.870
Foul!

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:11.130
Ball!

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:13.540
Foul!

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:15.820
Ball!

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:19.210
Foul!

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:26.100
B-Ball!

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:27.010
B-Ball!

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:27.930
Four balls!

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:29.240
All right!

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:30.840
You chose well, Miyazaki!

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:33.140
All right, let's start with one run.

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:35.990
Let's get one run back at a time!

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:41.730
Out!

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:43.230
Nice bunt!

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:45.240
It's our chance to score a run!

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:49.010
Batting eighth: center fielder, Takahashi-kun.

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:54.660
Out!

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:56.620
Don't mind, don't mind!

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:57.340
It's all right.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:10:00.270
Batting ninth: right fielder, Noguchi-kun.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:58.430
Keep it going! Do something!

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:04.130
You can hit it, Noguchi!

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.220
Strike!

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:12.760
<i>It's no good. I won't be able to hit these pitches...</i>

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:15.670
<i>But... I have to do something.</i>

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:18.370
<i>If I'm able to keep it going to Taiga...</i>

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:22.410
<i>Seeing how he is, even if we throw it inside,</i>

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:24.440
<i>we won't need to worry about getting hit.</i>

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:32.430
Dead ball!

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:38.160
<i>He got hit on purpose.</i>

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:43.020
Batting first: pitcher, Shimizu-kun.

00:10:43.020 --> 00:10:44.470
Hey! What're you doing!?

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:46.230
Taiga, isn't that you?

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:51.500
<i>Why is it?</i>

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:55.560
<i>Even though there's no guarantee I'll be able to hold them down and keep them from scoring runs...</i>

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:57.700
We're counting on you, Taiga!

00:10:57.700 --> 00:10:59.770
You can do it!

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:02.730
<i>Why won't everyone give up?</i>

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:06.150
<i>Are they stupid!?</i>

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:12.370
Slide, Miyazaki!

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:26.340
Out!

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:30.050
So close!

00:11:30.050 --> 00:11:30.600
Damn!

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:32.360
Jeez.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:38.480
Nice batting, Shimizu-kun.

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:43.440
We didn't score any runs, but there's a possibility for a comeback.

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:47.580
If I don't let them score any more runs, we'll be able to do something somehow.

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:53.360
What are you doing? It's time to change.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:57.030
I'm... looking for something.

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:02.020
Don't mind, don't mind. We'll score runs next time!

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:05.330
Yeah, let's keep them from getting any more runs!

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:09.630
Who're you!?

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:12.010
It's me... me.

00:12:12.010 --> 00:12:14.580
M-Miyazaki? Don't scare us.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:16.510
What happened to your glasses?

00:12:16.950 --> 00:12:20.350
I stepped on it, and one of the lenses broke.

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:22.250
What should I do?

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:25.640
I... can't see the ball without my glasses.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:26.970
What!?

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:29.460
You don't have spare glasses or anything?

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:30.650
N-No...

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:32.170
What're we going to do?

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:34.400
We don't have any members to switch in!

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:38.280
W-Well, I'll just play like this for the time being.

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:40.200
Hey, you.

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:42.590
Try catching this.

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:46.310
Ouch!

00:12:46.310 --> 00:12:47.850
H-Huh?

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:50.920
It's a disappointment, but in your condition,

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:53.760
I'm afraid I can't allow you to play.

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:55.500
How can this be?

00:12:55.500 --> 00:13:00.310
B-But we don't have another player to switch in.

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:04.770
Isn't there?

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:07.610
N-Nogoro-kun.

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:12.760
Number 10, Shigeno. Entering as first baseman.

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:18.280
This is a free fansub.

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:18.280
Not for sale or rent.

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.180
H-Hey,

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:22.480
is your foot all right, Shigeno?

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:25.800
You're in no condition to play yet, right?

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:31.130
Leave it to me. If it's just first, it's no big deal.

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:33.540
Wait a second, Nogoro-kun.

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:38.090
I haven't said that I would put you in yet.

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:41.160
Now's not the time to be saying that, is it?

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:44.100
At this rate, we're going to have to forfeit!

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:49.020
Even so, I think it's something that can't be helped.

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.110
Forfeit?

00:13:58.390 --> 00:13:59.940
H-Hey,

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:02.840
everyone worked so hard to get here,

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:07.040
and darling's saying that he'll be all right, so to forfeit is...

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:09.290
I'll play after all!

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:13.480
You'll get in trouble with the umpire again, Miyazaki-senpai!

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:17.130
But, at this rate, we just can't quit!

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:20.480
You won't allow me to play no matter what?

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:27.530
I understand.

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:32.110
However, Nogoro-kun, if I think that you are acting strangely at all,

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:36.190
I'll exercise my own judgment and forfeit the game immediately.

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:43.700
Seishuu High School: replacing first baseman Miyazaki-kun,

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:45.350
Shigeno-kun. 

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:47.250
Honda-kun?

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:49.710
Honda's on first?

00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:53.000
Huh? Isn't Honda-kun injured?

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:56.710
We need to test that.

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:08.480
Noguchi! You're too far back! You can stand further up!

00:15:08.480 --> 00:15:09.390
Y-Yes!

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:15.270
Fuji, I'll cover the area in between first and second. Lean more towards second.

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:16.110
A-All right.

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:18.740
In between second and third, play closer together!

00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:22.490
Left! We need to watch out for singles rather than deep hits right now!

00:15:22.490 --> 00:15:23.070
Yes!

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:24.550
Taiga!

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:28.910
You haven't even pitched 50 pitches. It's too early to get tired.

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:30.470
Put all you've got into it!

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:35.440
Huh? But it should've passed 70 pitches by now.

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:38.330
That's true.

00:15:39.630 --> 00:15:40.920
<i>I see.</i>

00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:42.780
Coach.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:44.600
Actually...

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:48.600
Strike!

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:51.010
Yes, I understand.

00:16:03.930 --> 00:16:04.620
Out!

00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:06.660
All right, one out!

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:06.660
I see.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:12.540
<i>With this person, restraint and holding back aren't necessary at all.</i>

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:15.550
Short!

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:19.090
Out!

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:23.050
Center!

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:27.810
Out!

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:30.520
All right! Nice, Takahashi!

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:32.400
Three outs! Change!

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:34.330
So close!

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:37.470
<i>I knew we couldn't take it easy.</i>

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:42.150
<i>With Honda-kun just standing on the field, Seishuu's movements have changed.</i>

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:45.410
<i>It's always been like that.</i>

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:51.620
<i>Being influenced by Honda-kun, everyone performs beyond their abilities.</i>

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:56.500
<i>That's why, in this inning...</i>

00:16:57.190 --> 00:16:59.960
<i>We mustn't allow Honda-kun to bat!</i>

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:02.360
Top of the sixth inning:

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:05.020
leading off for Seishuu High School...

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:08.150
Batting second: third baseman, Uchiyama-kun.

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:11.930
All right! Let's get some runs this inning!

00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:14.350
Go, Uchiyama!

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:18.670
Strike!

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:21.610
<i>I've got to get on base somehow!</i>

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:27.740
<i>If I get on base, it should become harder for them to walk Tashiro.</i>

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:35.410
Out!

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:39.130
I'm sorry.

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:42.380
Batting third: catcher, Tashiro-kun.

00:17:47.550 --> 00:17:50.370
Damn! They're walking him after all!

00:17:50.370 --> 00:17:52.600
Let's have a showdown, you cowards!

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:57.150
Ball!

00:17:57.150 --> 00:17:58.040
Four balls!

00:17:59.920 --> 00:18:02.540
<i>Thanks to the second batter's at-bat, it helped us.</i>

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:05.180
<i>With this, if we can strike out the fourth and fifth batters,</i>

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:06.990
<i>we won't get to Honda-kun.</i>

00:18:11.810 --> 00:18:13.370
<i>Damn!</i>

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:16.720
<i>I definitely won't allow you guys to have your way!</i>

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:24.660
Strike! Batter out!

00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:34.960
Batting fifth: shortstop, Hattori-kun.

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:38.430
<i>If we end it here, the next inning will begin with Honda-kun.</i>

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:42.860
<i>Even if we walk Honda-kun, we won't have a problem dealing with the batters after him.</i>

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:49.360
Run, Hattori!

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:53.330
Safe!

00:18:53.970 --> 00:18:54.980
He's fast!

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:57.290
As expected from a former track team member...

00:18:56.220 --> 00:18:57.290
Good job, Hattori!

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:02.880
Batting sixth: first baseman, Shigeno-kun.

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:04.840
All right!

00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:08.580
T-Time!

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:09.630
T-Time!

00:19:12.220 --> 00:19:15.310
What!? Walk Honda?

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:19.980
If you consider the risk of going up against Honda-kun,

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:23.150
it's safer striking out the next batter instead.

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:26.330
Now's not the time to be hesitating.

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:29.400
Wait, Komori...

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:32.450
There's a three-run difference.

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.660
I know why you're so wary of him,

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:39.410
but don't you want to battle him?

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:41.870
I do.

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:45.480
I do, but if we lose, it's over.

00:19:45.480 --> 00:19:48.650
In order not to let these past three years of hard work go to waste...

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:50.910
I see.

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:55.880
So you've decided on a plan against me?

00:19:58.310 --> 00:19:59.510
What!?

00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:00.770
They're walking him!?

00:20:01.310 --> 00:20:02.730
What are you doing?

00:20:03.230 --> 00:20:05.310
Yeah, actually face him!

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:05.980
Ball.

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:09.010
I'm sorry, Honda-kun.

00:20:09.010 --> 00:20:11.030
It's fine if you despise me.

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:12.670
Despise?

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:15.980
That's one of the great strategies, isn't it?

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:19.370
The only one who'd get angry over that would be a kid.

00:20:20.430 --> 00:20:21.410
But even so,

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:24.790
I'm still a kid!

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:26.590
A-A ball?

00:20:26.590 --> 00:20:27.840
He hit it!

00:20:29.340 --> 00:20:30.380
Go around!

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:31.380
G-Go around! 

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:32.360
Go around!

00:20:32.360 --> 00:20:32.880
Go around!

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:34.340
Run one!

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:36.550
Run two!

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:42.100
W-Why are they stopping?

00:20:45.750 --> 00:20:48.760
Unfortunately, that... is an out. 

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:50.110
"That"?

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:52.660
Hey, hey! What's going on!?

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:53.890
Why are we changing!?

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:56.630
None of the runners are out!

00:20:56.630 --> 00:20:58.050
The person that's out is you.

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:00.790
I was watching carefully.

00:21:01.580 --> 00:21:05.000
The batter cannot step out of the batter's box and hit the ball.

00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:09.600
Baseball Rules, 6.06.

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:14.320
"In the case that the batter steps one foot,
or both feet out of the batter's box and hits..." 

00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:15.760
It's against the rules.

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:22.980
If the bat hits the ball, regardless of whether it's fair or foul, the batter is out.

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:26.900
Did you not know that and jump out?

00:21:30.980 --> 00:21:33.480
Well, if it's the rule, then there's nothing I can do about it.

00:21:34.930 --> 00:21:37.770
So in the end, those two runs are just a dream?

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:39.340
Don't mind, don't mind!

00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:41.740
We've still got three innings!

00:21:42.130 --> 00:21:45.030
So Honda-kun didn't even know about that rule.

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:48.440
No, he probably knew and did it.

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:49.550
Why?

00:21:49.550 --> 00:21:55.090
Well, he might've been hoping that the umpire wouldn't notice.

00:21:55.790 --> 00:22:01.100
It's probably his silent protest against our cowardly battery.

00:22:03.610 --> 00:22:07.230
Bottom of the sixth inning: leading off for Mifune High School...

00:22:07.230 --> 00:22:10.900
Batting fourth: catcher, Komori-kun.

00:22:11.420 --> 00:22:13.370
<i>You've got to be joking.</i>

00:22:13.370 --> 00:22:15.990
<i>It's not like I'm walking him because I want to.</i>

00:22:16.800 --> 00:22:20.160
<i>I can't betray the hopes of the school and everyone.</i>

00:22:21.040 --> 00:22:22.370
<i>We...</i>

00:22:22.370 --> 00:22:25.830
<i>can't lose at a place like this!</i>

00:22:27.660 --> 00:22:28.170
It got through!

00:22:31.140 --> 00:22:32.050
Shigeno!

00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:34.090
That guy... He's going for the cut-off?

00:22:34.090 --> 00:22:35.730
Go around, Komori!

00:22:35.730 --> 00:22:37.050
You can get to third!

00:22:37.050 --> 00:22:38.090
Over here!

00:22:38.090 --> 00:22:38.930
Okay!

00:22:40.100 --> 00:22:43.640
I can't allow you to get any more runs!

00:22:53.680 --> 00:22:55.170
What an amazing shoulder...

00:22:55.170 --> 00:22:57.940
If he'd went for third, he would've been out.

00:22:58.750 --> 00:23:02.410
<i>It was in my calculations... that shoulder.</i>

00:23:03.760 --> 00:23:06.180
<i>Not bad, my childhood friend.</i>

00:24:40.960 --> 00:24:44.970
Because of Fuji's mistake, Seishuu gives up a fourth depressing run.

00:24:44.970 --> 00:24:46.850
But the game isn't over yet!

00:24:46.850 --> 00:24:48.510
I'll get it back with my bat!

00:24:49.130 --> 00:24:51.930
Face me, Yamane! Komori!

00:24:52.740 --> 00:24:54.130
Next time, on Major:

00:24:54.130 --> 00:24:55.850
Willpower vs. Willpower.

00:24:55.850 --> 00:24:57.980
Run to the stage of your dreams!
